# append_to_local_inbox bypasses the broker per-inbox lock — inbound relay DMs duplicated or silently lost

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Inbound relay DMs can be duplicated or silently lost. C2c_relay_connector.append_to_local_inbox (c2c_relay_connector.ml:909-927) does an unlocked read-merge-tmp-rename on <sid>.inbox.json while every broker drain path runs under with_inbox_lock (c2c_broker.ml:2215; drain_inbox at 3497, drain_inbox_push, drain_inbox_matching). (a) connector reads [X] -> MCP poll_inbox drains (archives X, saves empty) -> connector writes [X @ new] -> X re-delivered and re-archived. (b) broker load_inbox reads [X] -> connector appends Y -> broker saves empty -> Y silently lost, and the relay poll is destructive so Y is gone - unrecoverable for --ephemeral rows. Millisecond window recurring every interval per registered session.

## Fix direction

Acquire the same <sid>.inbox.json.lock sidecar (fcntl lockf, matching with_inbox_lock) around the merge, or hand inbound rows to a Broker API that already holds it.

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator (no lock in append_to_local_inbox).